# Kodiak's merge-queue config -- an unreviewed edit here could weaken or
# disable branch-protection-equivalent merge gating (e.g. the automerge
# label, blocking labels, or merge method).
/.kodiak.toml @derivita/technical-leadership-council

# This file decides what gets labeled `dependabot-automerge` (and
# therefore auto-approved), including the ecosystem allow-list -- an
# unreviewed edit could widen `ecosystems` to cover something not vetted
# for auto-merge.
/.github/workflows/dependabot-automerge-label.yml @derivita/technical-leadership-council

# Defines this repo's required status check ("runner / tests") -- the
# actual safety net once a PR is in Kodiak's scope. An unreviewed edit
# could weaken or remove it without anyone noticing.
/.github/workflows/ci.yml @derivita/technical-leadership-council

# CODEOWNERS must own itself -- otherwise any entry above can be deleted
# in an ordinary, unreviewed PR.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @derivita/technical-leadership-council

# NOTE: /.github/ is NOT owned wholesale (beyond the gate files above),
# unlike derivita/infrastructure's CODEOWNERS (which owns all of /.github/
# and therefore excludes github-actions from Kodiak auto-merge entirely).
# This repo's workflows are CI/build-only -- no deploy step, no secrets
# beyond GITHUB_TOKEN -- so owning all of /.github/ would only add
# friction to routine Actions-version bumps with no corresponding safety
# benefit. Mirrors derivita/shared-workflows' own CODEOWNERS pattern; see
# derivita/infrastructure#1719 for the fleet-wide risk audit this is
# based on.
